          "worked": "Divide each class frequency by 100 to find its relative frequency. Add class frequencies in order to find cumulative frequencies.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} A&=\\frac{18}{100}\\\\ A&=0.18\\\\ B&=\\frac{25}{100}\\\\ B&=0.25\\\\ C&=18+25\\\\ C&=43\\\\ D&=63-43\\\\ D&=20\\\\ E&=\\frac{17}{100}\\\\ E&=0.17\\\\ F&=80+20\\\\ F&=100 \\end{align*}$$",
